                  bab: "Medium",
                  fort: "Poor",
                  ref: "Poor",
                  will: "Good",
                  classSkills: ["Craft", "Fly", "Handle Animal", "Knowledge (arcana)", "Knowledge (planes)", "Linguistics", "Profession", "Ride", "Spellcraft", "Use Magic Device"],
                  summary: "A revised summoner with a separate eidolon spell list and a more balanced power level.",
                  desc: """
                  The Unchained Summoner was designed to address the balance concerns of the original summoner, primarily the eidolon's extreme power and the summoner's access to the full spell list. The unchained version separates the summoner and eidolon onto different power tracks.
                  
                  The eidolon now uses a dedicated eidolon spell list that is less comprehensive than before, and the eidolon's evolution point system has been rebalanced. Evolutions work similarly to before but with adjusted costs and effects. The summoner still merges with the eidolon at high levels.
                  
                  The unchained summoner's own spell list has been trimmed and now focuses more on conjuration and planar magic. Summon Monster as a spell-like ability remains, providing battlefield control through summoned creatures. The overall result is a class that remains powerful and unique while being less capable of dominating encounters through the eidolon alone.
